// THE SHIPPED DEFAULT of the row_house_three_bedroom (2026-11-13, docs/design/home-room-program.md). Compiled
// into the exe (crates/humanity-core/src/embedded_data.rs `shipped_home_design`) and never written by
// the game: a neighbour's plot of this kind is drawn as it (crates/humanity-ship/src/neighbours.rs),
// and a game with no data/homes/row_house_three_bedroom.ron of its own starts its home from it. YOUR home is
// data/homes/row_house_three_bedroom.ron, which every editor Save rewrites; it starts as a copy of this file WITHOUT
// this paragraph (`own_home_text` drops everything from the first line down to the bare // below).
// To change the default every newcomer gets, edit this file (keeping this paragraph on top) and
// rebuild: data/homes/shipped is in build.rs FINGERPRINT_INPUTS, so a rig refuses an exe built
// before the edit. Then redraw it: `node scripts/draw-homes.js <folder>`.
//
// HumanityOS home design: the ROW HOUSE WITH THREE BEDROOMS FOR FIVE (2026-11-13, docs/design/home-room-program.md
// section 10), one home of a terrace on Row Street (data/blueprints/ship_structure.ron). A draft for
// developers (data/homes/starts.ron, `dev: true`).
//
// Three bedrooms for five on two storeys: the space standard asks 93 m2 (3b5p, two storeys), two
// doubles or twins of 11.5 m2 (one at least 2.75 m wide, the other 2.55 m) and a single of 7.5 m2,
// 2.15 m wide. Wider, not taller: 6.5 m of frontage instead of a third storey, which would need a
// second flight beside the first (a 2 m stair on a 5.5 m frontage), 99 m2 instead of 93, and a 9 m
// plot over its 6 m neighbours. Plot 6.5 x 18 m = 117 m2; house 6.5 x 9.5 m, 123.5 m2 gross; yard
// 6.5 x 6.5 m = 42 m2. Ground: hall and stair 4.5 x 2 m, living room 4.5 x 4.5 m at the front, a WC
// 2 x 2 m off the hall (five people and one bathroom), a utility 3 x 2 m (laundry, the ship's
// hookups, the back door) and the kitchen and dining 5 x 4.5 m opening on the yard. Upper: the
// single 4.5 x 2.5 m and the front double 4.5 x 3 m over the living room, the back double 3.5 x 4 m
// and the bathroom 3.5 x 2.5 m over the kitchen, the landing across the middle.
//
// Frame as the homesteads': the street is west, the door in the west wall, x the distance from the
// street, z along it. The side walls of the house are the party walls (the plot's shell); the
// gardens' edges are OPEN (`open_shell`): the yards behind a terrace are one green, each plot's
// north line marked by a mowing strip, the street edge a 0.9 m front garden wall with the gate.
// Every bedroom meets England's space standard inside its walls and every room is reached, lit and
// found by the game (crates/humanity-ship/src/home_program_tests.rs).
//
// Materials: 1 = steel (the shell), 2 = concrete, 3 = wood, 4 = glass, 9 = steel balustrade.
